# The words of story parts that are no longer parts (see moved.map): found ones keep them, so the lore book and the
# armour stand still read them. Never handed out again. "id | item | name | text".
x:a:lantern:2 | bow | Mothsparer | M. could hit a moth at forty paces. She never did; she liked moths. She shot only once in anger, the night the ships stopped coming.
x:a:lantern:3 | iron_axe | The Beam-Cutter | Maren cut the lighthouse beams herself, one winter, alone. The sea took the lighthouse anyway, but it took forty years and it had to try very hard.
x:a:lantern:4 | trident | Where the Light Went Out | Carried out of the sea by a drowned, from the very spot where the lantern fell. It is still faintly warm, as if something down there is keeping it lit.
x:a:lantern:5 | crossbow | Oskar's Grudge | Her brother Oskar's. He never forgave the sea, and the sea never apologised. He sat on the cliffs with this every night, waiting for it to try.
x:a:ninth:5 | wooden_hoe | Last Harvest | The fields of the Ninth Village were tilled with this the day before. The crops still come up every spring, in perfect rows, for nobody.
x:a:ninth:6 | shears | The Bell-Rope | Used to cut the bell-rope after the ninth ring. It didn't help. The bell kept ringing with no rope at all.
x:a:ninth:7 | shield | The Village Banner | It still carries the banner of a village that is on no map. Show it to an old villager and watch them go very quiet.
x:a:pell:1 | wooden_hoe | The Pie Garden | Grandma Pell grows the pumpkins for her famous pies with this. Nobody has ever seen a pumpkin seed in her garden. They have seen a lot of very nervous travellers.
x:a:pell:2 | iron_axe | The Rolling Pin | It's an axe, but Grandma Pell calls it her rolling pin, and nobody has ever been brave enough to correct her.
x:a:pell:6 | fishing_rod | The Swamp Line | Pell fishes in the swamp behind her cottage. She says she catches catfish. The catfish are not fish. The catfish are not cats.
x:a:crumb:3 | bow | Crumb's Hopeful Bow | Tobias fired three hundred arrows with this and hit one target: himself. Twice. He says it was a tactic.
x:a:crumb:5 | wooden_pickaxe | Crumb's Lucky Pick | He mined straight down with this, which everyone tells you never to do, and landed in a pile of diamonds. Then a pile of lava. Then, luckily, a pile of water.
x:a:crumb:6 | fishing_rod | Crumb's Big Catch | Tobias claims he caught a dragon with this. It was a squid. It was a small squid. It got away.
x:a:crumb:8 | flint_and_steel | Crumb's Campfire | Tobias tried to light a cosy campfire with this once. The forest is still recovering. So are his eyebrows.
x:a:torch:7 | crossbow | The Torch-Bearer's Answer | Used to fire burning bolts into the dark. The dark did not care about fire. The dark cared about noise.
x:a:choir:6 | bow | The Silence Bow | When a Choir member broke the song, the archer took care of the silence. The archer never missed. The silence was always complete.
x:a:cartographer:5 | fishing_rod | Line of Depths | Ilse used this to measure the depth of the sea, by lowering the line until it stopped. One day it didn't stop.
x:a:twins:5 | shield | The Fake Crest | A noble family's crest, painted on by the twins to sell it to the noble family. The noble family bought it. They're very proud. They don't know.
x:a:twins:6 | flint_and_steel | Twin Flames | The twins once sold a village "fire insurance" and then made very sure the village needed it. They ran with this. They are no longer welcome on the coast.
x:a:quiet:3 | bow | Arrow to the Moon | A hunter fired an arrow into the quiet sky that winter to see if anything was there. Something was. It sent the arrow back.
x:a:halvard:6 | shield | The Last Wall | The Sunken Hall's last wall was a line of shields. This was in the middle. The water came over the top, as water does.
x:a:firsttools:1 | wooden_pickaxe | Pip's First Pick | Pip was seven and made this pickaxe all by herself, with only a little bit of help, which was mostly her dad doing it. She mined one block of stone and was a miner from that day on.
x:a:firsttools:2 | wooden_axe | Pip's First Axe | She chopped her first tree with this. It took all afternoon. She came home covered in sawdust and said trees were "very rude" for being so hard. Then she went back for another.
x:a:firsttools:3 | stone_pickaxe | Pip's Real Pick | At ten she made a stone pickaxe with no help at all and wouldn't let anyone else touch it. She dug a cellar under the shed. Nobody knew until the shed sank a little.
x:a:outpostledger:2 | crossbow | Ledger, Page Two | Income: 1 allay (complaining). Expenses: 1 cage (allay escaped through the bars), 2 guards (fired), 1 cage (allay-proof, pending). Morale: low. Allay: thriving.
x:a:outpostledger:4 | crossbow | Ledger, Final Page | Income: none. Expenses: entire outpost (a hero of the village was involved). Note for next quarter: build the outpost further from the village. Note two: any further.
x:a:breeze:2 | shield | Toy Number Two | It used the shield as a sled down the copper stairs. Shields are not sleds. The breeze didn't know that. The breeze didn't know very much. It had a wonderful time.
x:a:breeze:3 | trident | Toy Number Three | It tried to throw the trident like the adventurers did. The trident went into the wall and stayed there for six years. The breeze was very patient. It waited. It was worth it.
x:a:fishinglessons:2 | fishing_rod | Mum's Rod | Mum cast like an arrow and reeled like a winch and caught three fish while Grandad caught a nap. She never told him. She put her fish in his bucket so he'd wake up proud.
x:a:ravagerrider:4 | iron_axe | Grimtusk's Retirement | When the raids stopped, Grimtusk and Petal moved to a farm by a village they'd once raided. The villagers were terrified for a year. Then Petal pulled their ploughs. Now they bring her apples.
x:a:ferryman:2 | stone_spear | The First Passenger's Spear | The first passenger left this in the boat, a stone spear, very old. He said he wouldn't need it on the other side. The ferryman kept it. He keeps everything they leave.
x:a:ferryman:3 | iron_spear | The Soldier's Spear | A soldier left this with a note: "for my son, if he ever comes this way, which I hope he won't for a long time". The ferryman has it ready. He hopes so too.
x:a:butler:1 | chainmail_chestplate | Chapter One: My Appointment | I entered the service of the mansion in my twenty-second year. The household consisted of forty-one evokers, two hundred vindicators and one very old allay who did the dusting. I wore chain, as the staff were frequently attacked by the family.
x:a:doctor:5 | iron_shovel | The Garden on the Hill | When it was over, the valley planted a garden on the hill, a flower for every name with a tick. It is a very big garden. The doctor's cap hangs on the gate.
x:a:bandit:2 | copper_spear | The Bridge-Keeper's Spear | Her right hand, Big Tobble, held the bridge with this. Nobody crossed without paying the toll. The toll was a joke. If it was funny, you crossed for free. Tobble had no sense of humour.
x:a:apprentice2:2 | wooden_hoe | Day 12 | Weeding the mandrake patch. Mistress says don't pull them up, they scream. I pulled one up. It screamed. I screamed. Mistress screamed at both of us. Nobody is speaking to anyone.
x:a:apprentice2:4 | fishing_rod | Day 59 | Fishing for a frog with a crown on, for a spell. Caught three ordinary frogs and one very indignant prince. Mistress says we'll "talk about the prince later".
x:a:golemfriend:5 | iron_boots | The New One | The village built a new golem. Lina, grown, put the old boots on its feet herself. The new golem looked down at her for a long time. Then it handed her a poppy.
x:a:goldsmith:2 | golden_shovel | The Shovel for the Princess | The princess ordered a golden shovel to plant a single tulip at her coronation. She used it once. Ferro had made it to last exactly one tulip. It lasted exactly one tulip.
x:a:goldsmith:3 | golden_hoe | The Hoe That Fed No One | Ferro's apprentice asked him why. Ferro said a farmer worked his whole life with ugly tools, and once, just once, he should hold something beautiful while he did it. He gave this to a farmer.
x:a:deepspear:2 | iron_spear | Her Old Spear | Before the diamond one, she had this. She buried it on an island with a map, so that one day a child would find it and want to be a princess of the sea too.
x:a:woodcarver:2 | copper_axe | The Axe She Gave Him | His wife gave him a proper copper axe on their thirtieth anniversary. He never used it. He said it was too nice. It hung over the fireplace, green, next to her picture.
x:a:woodcarver:3 | stone_axe | The Spare He Lent Out | Any child who wanted to learn carving could borrow this. Most of them cut their thumb on the first day. All of them came back on the second. That's how you know who'll be a carver.
x:a:spearfisher:3 | stone_spear | The Teaching Spear | The first spear every child at Kelp Point gets is stone, so it doesn't matter if they throw it into the deep. Most of them do. The deep is full of stone spears. The fish build houses with them.
x:a:diamondtools:2 | diamond_shovel | Mira's Spade | She dug a tunnel through the mountain with this so the children of the far valley could get to school in winter. It took her nine years. The tunnel is still called Mira's Shortcut.
x:a:diamondtools:3 | diamond_axe | Mira's Axe | She cut the beams for the tunnel with this, one by one, and carved a child's name into each beam, every child who'd walk through. There are two hundred and twelve names.
x:a:gilded:2 | golden_axe | The Collector's Axe | Grashk's brute cousin collects debts with this. The debt is still one gold ingot. The interest is now everything you own.
x:a:ashgrove:6 | wooden_hoe | The Village Garden | Back home, Ashgrove's village planted a garden for his return. It is still tended. Somebody comes at night and waters it. Nobody knows who.
x:a:wren:6 | fishing_rod | Holloway's Anchor | She used this to fish passing parrots out of the air for her crew. Her crew was all parrots. Things were complicated on her ship.
x:a:glasswidow:2 | iron_shovel | Black Sand | She dug soul sand from the edge of a portal with this, to make the window herself. The glass came out dark, and in it, sometimes, she could see him waving.
x:a:wellroot:2 | iron_shovel | Upper Wellroot's Moat | Upper Wellroot dug a moat to keep the Lower Wellrooters out. It was knee-deep. Everybody stepped over it. It was still a point of pride.
x:a:wellroot:3 | iron_sword | Lower Wellroot's Pride | The finest sword in Lower Wellroot. It was used in the Wellroot War exactly once, to cut the ribbon of the peace banquet.
x:a:wellroot:5 | bow | The Archer of Both Wellroots | The only archer in either village. He fought for both sides on alternate days and got paid twice. He's the only one who misses the war.
x:a:goat:5 | wooden_hoe | The Prophet's Feast | The followers grew wheat with this to feed the Goat Prophet. He ate the wheat, the hoe's handle, and the farmer's hat.
x:a:marrow:4 | bow | The Fourth Debt | An arrow that never misses. He used it once, on the witch's crow, so she wouldn't see him leave. She saw.
x:a:marrow:6 | shield | The Sixth Debt | One more day. That's all he asked for. She gave him the shield and the day. He spent the day running.
x:a:obsidianheart:5 | diamond_shovel | The Burial | They buried the obsidian heart back where they found it. It's very quiet there now. Miners still won't dig within a mile.
x:a:whisperwood:2 | bow | The Dryad's Bow | Made from the first tree Kett felled in the Whisperwood. It shoots true. When it hits, you hear a sigh.
x:a:whisperwood:3 | shears | Leaf-Taker | Used to trim the hedges around the Whisperwood so nobody wandered in. One night, the hedges trimmed back.
x:a:amberlight:1 | crossbow | The Human Cannonball's Crossbow | The Amberlight Circus fired its star act from a giant crossbow. This is the smaller practice version. The practice volunteer was a very surprised chicken.
x:a:beekeeper:4 | iron_sword | The Hornet's Answer | When raiders came to Honeyhollow, Agnes didn't fight. She just opened the hives. This sword belonged to the raider who was stung least. He was stung a lot.
x:a:oldbuilders:3 | iron_shovel | Foundation Spade | Dug up beneath a ruin older than the ruin above it. The Old Builders built on top of their own buildings, as if they were hiding the first ones.
x:a:crimsonbard:5 | shield | The Bard's Last Stage | Used as a stage for his final show, by a lava lake. The scorch marks are his footprints, dancing.
x:a:bluecheese:3 | iron_sword | The Inside Man | The guard who let the thieves in was paid in cheese. He swore it was the best day of his life. It was also the last day of his job.
x:a:bluecheese:4 | shears | The Rope Cutters | They lowered the cheese from the tower on a rope. These cut the rope. Too early. The cheese rolled down the mountain and through three villages. It is still rolling, they say.
x:a:sculkchild:5 | bow | What She Heard | She said the Warden dreams about the surface. It wants to see the sun. That's why it's so angry about noise: it's trying to hear the birds.
x:a:mire:3 | wooden_hoe | The Toad Garden | Agatha grew mushrooms, warts and one lettuce, out of spite. This hoe tended them. The lettuce is still alive. Nobody is allowed to eat it.
x:a:mire:6 | fishing_rod | Agatha's Wishing Line | She fished in the mire for wishes. She caught three. She used one on a better cauldron, one on a cat, and kept the last one in a jar. The jar is missing.
x:a:clocktower:3 | iron_sword | The Hand of the Hour | Made from the clock's hour hand after it fell. It still points at one o'clock, whichever way you hold it.
x:a:lostlegion:5 | crossbow | The Last Order | Found with a note: "Halt." The legion's runner had been carrying it the whole time. He was too polite to interrupt.
x:a:deepfisher:5 | iron_sword | The Daughter's Answer | She went down after him with this, against all advice. She came back with his hat and a look on her face. She never fished again.
x:a:bramble:2 | iron_shovel | Bramble's Second Shovel | Nobody knows what happened to the first shovel. Bramble only ever said "the mountain kept it".
x:a:hollowfarm:4 | stone_axe | The Fence-Mender | Used to mend fences the cows had broken. The cows broke them again. It was a long, friendly war.
x:a:digsite:2 | iron_shovel | The Dunmarrow Spade | Used to dig the first trench at Dunmarrow, where the Old Builders' town lay under the dunes. The town was there. So was something else.
x:a:chef:2 | wooden_hoe | The Herb Garden Hoe | Used in the royal herb garden. The king never knew where the parsley came from. The gardener never told him; she liked the mystery.
x:a:chef:5 | iron_sword | The Carving Sword | Used to carve the roast at the king's feast. The roast was a whole cow. The sword was the only knife big enough.
x:a:moonfarmer:5 | stone_axe | The Shed Axe | Used to build his shed, his fence and his small but deeply unsettling scarecrow army.
x:a:greenhero:3 | bow | The Hero's Bow | He used it to hit switches nobody else could reach. Every switch opened a door. Every door had a key behind it. He was very good at keys.
x:a:aldo:2 | stone_axe | The Spare Axe | Aldo kept a stone axe by the door "for when the good one breaks". It never did. His granddaughter learned to chop with this one, standing on a stump so she could reach.
x:a:pilgrim:6 | golden_pickaxe | The Pick That Cleared the Way | Found at the fifth portal, which had collapsed from the other side. The flower was pressed flat between two pages of a letter. It still smelled of the Nether.
x:a:grashk2:5 | crossbow | The Royal Guard's Bow | Fired only at people who forgot to wear gold. It was fired a great deal. Humans have very bad memories.
x:a:charred:2 | stone_sword | The Second Blade | Here lieth the blade of Varn, who laughed the loudest, and was the first to go silent. The smoke hath not dimmed the edge. It remembereth his laugh, though he doth not.
x:a:charred:3 | stone_sword | The Third Blade | Edda carried this, who had a daughter in the green lands above. She asked of each traveller whether the grass was still soft. None who came would answer. She asketh still, without a voice.
x:a:charred:4 | stone_sword | The Fourth Blade | The fourth never wanted to come. He swore because his brother swore. His brother fell on the first night. He hath stood at the gate ever since, guarding a promise that was never his.
x:a:charred:5 | stone_sword | The Fifth Blade | Blackened, nicked, and wrapped at the grip with a scrap of blue cloth. Blue was not a colour of the Nether. Someone brought it from home, and kept it, all this while.
x:a:saltreach:2 | trident | Little Pell's Spear | The youngest deckhand had never held a weapon. He took this from the hold when the ship began to tip, because he thought it would make him brave. It did. It didn't help.
x:a:saltreach:4 | fishing_rod | The Bosun's Spare Rod | The bosun lent this to every sailor who was homesick, because fishing is the same on every sea. He said it helps. Down there, he still holds it out to anyone passing by.
x:a:saltreach:5 | trident | The Lookout's Trident | The lookout saw the reef too late. She has looked up at the surface every day since, as if she might see the next ship in time. Sometimes she does. Sometimes they listen.
x:a:coppercamp:2 | copper_sword | My Sword (Mine) | Day three. I got my own sword because I'm eleven now. It's copper so it turns green, which Dad says means it's "doing its best". I fought a bush. I won.
x:a:coppercamp:3 | copper_spear | The Fishing Spear | Day five. Mum spears fish with this standing in the river like a heron. She caught seven. I caught a boot. Dad says the boot was "a strong start".
x:a:deepvein:2 | iron_pickaxe | Memo No. 4 | To all crews: the east wall is not to be mined further until further notice. Crew 3 is reminded that "it asked us to stop" is not an approved reason for leaving a shift early. Management.
x:a:deepvein:3 | iron_pickaxe | Memo No. 7 | To all crews: Crew 3's picks have been found. Crew 3 has not. The company thanks Crew 3 for its service. The east wall is to be bricked up by Friday. Management.
x:a:yrsa:1 | iron_axe | Her Father's Axe | Yrsa grew up in the outpost, among people who took things from villages. Her father gave her this axe on her tenth birthday and said "now you are one of us". She hid it under her bed.
x:a:yrsa:2 | crossbow | The Crossbow She Didn't Fire | On her first raid she raised this at a farmer's boy her own age. He looked at her. She looked at him. She lowered it and ran into the forest, and she did not stop.
x:a:trialwardens:3 | bow | The Archer of Hall Seven | "In Hall Seven, a bow that never missed! Except once! At the announcer! THE ANNOUNCER IS FINE! THE ANNOUNCER WOULD LIKE TO MOVE ON!"
x:a:trialwardens:4 | crossbow | The Bolt of the Final Round | "The final round! A single bolt! The vault key on a pressure plate! Ladies and gentlemen and breezes, I have never seen a crossbow aimed with so much love!"
x:a:trialwardens:5 | shield | The Shield of the Runner-Up | "The runner-up! Held this shield for forty minutes against six spawners! Lost on a technicality! The technicality was a slime! A standing ovation for the runner-up!"
x:a:gardener:3 | diamond_leggings | The Watcher's Greaves | Someone else's, left beside the garden wall. The Warden walked past this garden for three hundred years and never once stepped on it. Nobody knows if it knew. Everybody hopes it did.
x:a:firstchest:3 | stone_pickaxe | The Second Pick | And the stone was made into a better pick, and with it the first of us went down into the dark, and found coal, and made light, and understood that there would be no end to digging.
x:a:firstchest:4 | stone_axe | The Axe That Built a House | And with this axe the first of us built a house of planks, just big enough for one, and slept there the first night, and heard the moaning outside, and was glad of the door.
x:a:stonesong:2 | stone_axe | Second Verse | Father built boats with this axe on the sand, the best boats in Saltmere, the best in the land; then the sea came up softly one night in the spring, and the boats were too slow for so big a thing.
x:a:archercorps:2 | bow | Private Femur | Private Femur once shot a creeper by accident and blew up his whole squad. He was given a medal, a demotion and a new squad, in that order. The new squad keeps its distance.
x:a:archercorps:3 | bow | Corporal Clatter | Clatter's arrows always went a bit to the left. He compensated by aiming a bit to the right. He has never hit anything. He has never stopped trying. The Corps respects that.
x:a:hagra:2 | iron_boots | Second Trade | "SAME BOOTS AGAIN. HUMAN BOUGHT BOOTS, HUMAN DROPPED BOOTS IN LAVA, HAGRA FISHED BOOTS OUT. ALMOST NEW. HOT. DO NOT PUT ON YET."
x:a:hagra:3 | iron_boots | Third Trade | "LAST BOOTS. HAGRA HAS NO MORE BOOTS. HAGRA HAS NEVER HAD BOOTS. HAGRA FINDS BOOTS. NOBODY ASKS WHERE. GOOD HUMAN. NO ASK."
x:a:smallthings:3 | bow | The Bow in the Water | Pulled up one morning on his line. Rosa's old bow, from when she was a girl and wanted to be an adventurer. He'd never known she had one. He sat on the jetty and laughed until he cried.
x:a:embergulch:2 | golden_shovel | The Claim Jumper's Spade | Snake-Eye Pete dug up three claims that weren't his with this here shovel. Then the fourth claim dug him up. That's the gulch for you. It gives and it takes and it don't explain.
x:a:embergulch:4 | golden_hoe | The Gold Farmer | One fella tried to plant gold nuggets in the dirt to grow more gold. Tilled the whole gulch with this golden hoe. Nothing grew. He's still waiting. Says it's a slow crop.
x:a:copperpot:6 | copper_axe | Copperpot's Retirement | He hung up his green armour and became a woodcutter in that village, and married the miller, and nobody ever told him his armour was the colour of a frog. They loved him for it.
x:a:spearmaidens:1 | stone_spear | Ninna's Spear | Hear now of the four sisters of the shallows, who fished with spears and feared no tide. The youngest, Ninna, bore stone, for she said a spear should be as patient as the sea floor.
x:a:spearmaidens:2 | copper_spear | Ada's Spear | The second, Ada, bore copper, which greeneth in the salt like weed upon a wreck. She said that a spear should belong to the sea, and the sea should know its own.
x:a:spearmaidens:3 | iron_spear | Ylva's Spear | The third, Ylva, bore iron, and she alone of the four was ever wounded, guarding her sisters from the drowned on the night the moon went dark. She spoke of it to no one.
x:a:ostra:2 | golden_hoe | The Golden One | Ostra's husband brought it back from his travels, a hoe of solid gold, completely useless for farming. She used it every day for forty years. Out of stubbornness and love, in about equal amounts.
x:a:ashmoor:3 | crossbow | The Judge's Crossbow | The fair judge, who had judged the contest for thirty years, finally fired a bolt into the target between them and said: "For goodness' sake, just get married." They did. They argued about the rabbit at the wedding.
x:a:ashmoor:4 | crossbow | The Children's Crossbow | Their daughter refused to learn the bow, out of spite, and became the best crossbow shot in the north. At the fair she beat both of them in one round. They have never been prouder or more annoyed.
x:a:notdiamond:2 | diamond_shovel | The Shovel of More | With his diamonds he made a shovel, to dig faster, so as to find more diamonds, to make more tools, to dig faster still. He forgot what the diamonds were for. He forgot to eat lunch.
x:a:notdiamond:3 | diamond_axe | The Axe of Alone | He cut down the trees around his house, so that no one could see his diamonds. Then there was no one to see them at all. He showed them to his own reflection. It was not impressed.
x:a:apprentice:2 | iron_axe | Practice Piece Two | "The head's on crooked," said her master. "It's on at a jaunty angle," said Wenna. He laughed so hard he burned his beard on the forge. He kept the axe. It chops wood just fine.
x:a:apprentice:3 | iron_pickaxe | Practice Piece Three | Her first pick that the miners actually wanted to buy. She sold it for three emeralds and then followed the miner to the mountain to watch it work. He let her watch for an hour.
x:a:apprentice:4 | iron_shovel | Practice Piece Four | She hid her mark on the inside of the socket, a tiny bird, where nobody would look. Her master found it at once. He said nothing. He added his own mark next to hers, an even tinier bird.
x:a:mapson:4 | bow | Bram's Bow | He grew up on the road. He learned the bow, the sea, the stars. In time he could read a coastline like a letter. People started asking him about the shape of the coast.
x:a:tridentkings:2 | trident | The King of the Coral | The second is the King of the Coral, bright and proud, who wanted the whole reef for a crown. He bore this. The reef is dying now, grey and quiet, and the King sits on it alone.
x:a:flintkeepers:2 | flint_and_steel | The Keeper Who Stayed | One Keeper stopped in a village where an old man lived alone, and lit his fire, and stayed to talk, and came back the next night, and the next, until the old man died warm.
